      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "title": "Why not just a page?",
        "body": "A page is the right form for something you read straight through, and Twilite keeps those too. A project is not read from top to bottom. What needs you today depends on which tasks are open, which questions are unanswered, and which goals they serve.\n\nIn a page, all of that lives in the prose, and you or your AI have to reread and re-sort it every time. In a graph the structure is already written down. Change one status and everything connected to it can see. Your AI can add a task without rewriting your document.\n\nAnd a graph still has a page: when you are close enough to read it, you see its first face.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "what-is-a-graph-demo"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      }
    },
